<p>Look at grind's row: it is essentially a bet on Thursday. It made +$704 there on 46 trades and lost on the two other days it fired at all. That is not a flaw — it's what the 0.35 ER floor is <em>for</em>, keeping it dormant unless the day really trends — but it does mean grind's +$184 for the week is one great day minus two poor ones, not a broad edge. Compare exhaustion's row: green four days out of five, never a monster but never a disaster until Friday's open. That row is why exhaustion is the survivor.</p>
